00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:10.400
MARK MANDEL: Awesome.

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:12.500
And finally, this is
something that I've actually

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:15.100
really wanted for a
really, really long time,

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:16.430
and I'm so glad to see it.

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:18.610
Cloud Scheduler is available.

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:20.950
So basically, if you've
ever wanted to run anything

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:23.080
on Google Cloud Platform
on a regular basis

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:25.900
without having to start
up a VM with Cron,

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:28.210
or just to create a
simple App Engine app just

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:31.000
to do Cron scripting, we now
have a thing that does this,

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:32.190
and it's really good.

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:33.430
So it's a job scheduler.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:35.860
You set it up-- it actually
uses the same Chrome tab-type

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:36.640
format.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.610
But basically, if you want
to push an event to an HTTP

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:41.140
endpoint or to
Pub/Sub, and you want

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.820
to do it on a regular
basis, you can now

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:44.414
do it through Cloud Scheduler.

00:05:44.414 --> 00:05:46.330
And you can go play with
it now, and it works,

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:47.380
and it does cool stuff.

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:49.880
So no more having to build these
little App Engine apps just

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:50.820
to do Cron stuff.

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:51.736
MICHELLE CASBON: Nice.

00:05:51.736 --> 00:05:54.820
So you can upload your
asterisk commands directly

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:56.320
to the Cloud
scheduler, and not have

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:58.210
to worry about building
a whole app around it.

00:05:58.210 --> 00:05:58.270
MARK MANDEL: Nope.

00:05:58.270 --> 00:05:59.040
You have to build the whole app.

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:00.250
It's just a little
